[38;5;252m[1m## The bug that mattered was in my harness, not the code[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The first full run passed immediately, which was suspicious. Mutation testing proved why: [38;5;10mcargo test[0m never builds the [38;5;10mcdylib[0m (no test target links it), so the harness was loading a [1mstale[22m [38;5;10m.so[0m and [1m16 of 17 injected bugs went undetected[22m. After changing the harness to unconditionally run [38;5;10mcargo build --lib[0m before loading, all 17 mutations are caught — wrong swap lanes, 12- vs 16-byte chunk stride, bit-cast instead of numeric conversion, swapped return codes, and more.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two artifacts at the repo root: [38;5;10mverify_all.sh[0m (enumerates feature combos from [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m, runs check/build/test/[38;5;10mnm[0m parity for each) and [38;5;10mmutation_check.sh[0m (guards against harness rot). [38;5;10mc_src/[0m is untouched.[0m[0m
